WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.684
WKS-TRN-07 is behaving strangely and we think it is infected.

2
00:00:05.684 --> 00:00:11.055
Performance criteria 3.3 and 3.4: check and patch the updates,

3
00:00:11.055 --> 00:00:16.166
then use the security solution to scan the infected system.

4
00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:20.152
Watch what happens if I take a shortcut first.

5
00:00:21.251 --> 00:00:23.359
First the versions.

6
00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:25.909
Signatures 1.421.112.0.

7
00:00:25.909 --> 00:00:35.669
The vendor bulletin says the latest is 1.421.130.0, so these signatures are out of date.

8
00:00:35.669 --> 00:00:41.435
The engine and platform versions match the bulletin.

9
00:00:42.535 --> 00:00:46.186
The shortcut: a quick scan with the old signatures.

10
00:00:46.186 --> 00:00:47.402
No threats found.

11
00:00:47.402 --> 00:00:54.345
It is tempting to write clean in the log, but a quick scan only looks in the usual hiding places,

12
00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:58.567
and yesterday's signatures do not know this week's threats.

13
00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.732
The SOP way.

14
00:01:01.732 --> 00:01:08.098
Rule V3: update the signatures first.

15
00:01:08.098 --> 00:01:14.979
They go from 1.421.112.0 to 1.421.130.0.

16
00:01:16.079 --> 00:01:20.643
Rule V4: on an infected system, run a full scan.

17
00:01:20.643 --> 00:01:25.871
This time Defender finds a threat: Trojan Win32 Vigorf.

18
00:01:26.971 --> 00:01:28.219
Now verify.

19
00:01:28.219 --> 00:01:33.209
The newest event first: scan finished, 1001.

20
00:01:33.209 --> 00:01:35.931
Then 1117, action taken.

21
00:01:35.931 --> 00:01:38.312
Then 1116, detection.

22
00:01:38.312 --> 00:01:43.075
The full scan found it and quarantined it.

23
00:01:44.175 --> 00:01:52.636
And the host itself: the file was in the user's AppData Roaming Updater folder, a place a quick scan does not check.

24
00:01:52.636 --> 00:01:55.990
Test-Path says False: the file is really gone.

25
00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.199
Now I can record the result with confidence.

26
00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:01.195
Your turn.

27
00:02:01.195 --> 00:02:04.507
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 8.

28
00:02:04.507 --> 00:02:11.758
In Activity 8.3, check the bank's update versions and patch your own workstation.

29
00:02:11.758 --> 00:02:20.620
Then in Activity 8.4, your workstation is infected: update, run a full scan, and verify the result.

30
00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.395
On some seats the action fails.

31
00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:25.811
If yours does, escalate it.

